# ADAPTER-DEPTH: issue 88's recipe knob, and the band coverage that keeps it honest

**Issue 88 cannot run without this.** `cli.py` set the LoRA config's `num_layers` to
`resolved.num_layers` unconditionally, so every run this repository has ever done adapted every
layer and there was no way to ask for fewer. The ablation is "a recipe variant, not a probe
variant", so the variant has to exist in the recipe.

## `train.lora_layers`

Absent, the depth is every layer — what every run before this did, and what R50 requires of any run
whose adapter will be read. Present, it is the number of **top** layers `linear_to_lora_layers`
adapts, so 8 on a 32-layer model means layers 25 to 32 and nothing below.

**Validated, not clamped.** A depth of 0, a negative, or one past the model's layer count is a typo
in a recipe, and silently training a different model than the config asked for is worse than
refusing before the weights load.

## The band coverage, because "most of the band" is the sentence to prevent

R41d makes a declared pair one unit whose members carry the same role, so **a split pair is not a
covered pair**. `_band_coverage` reports whole pairs, split pairs with the member that fell
outside, and pairs entirely outside. On the 4B's five pairs:

| depth | lowest adapted layer | whole | split |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| top 8 | 25 | 27/28 — **one of five** | none |
| top 16 | 17 | 19/20, 23/24, 27/28 — **three of five** | 16/17, with 17 in and 16 out |
| all 32 | 1 | all five | none |

It is recorded at every depth, including full, so a reader never infers coverage from
`num_layers`, and it goes to both the run log and the provenance rather than only one.

## The pairs come from the registry

`probes.live_lens_pairs` was declared in `configs/models/qwen35-4b.yaml` and read only by
`live_lens.instruments.read_band`, which validates against the installed block kinds and therefore
needs a loaded model. This adds `spec.probes.live_lens_pairs` for readers that need the
**declaration** rather than the validation — a second copy of the pairs beside the code that reports
them is how the band ruling and the code drift apart. `read_band` is unchanged and remains the
validating reader.

## One thing I nearly shipped by accident, stated

`ruff check --fix` on `cli.py` removed the module-scope `render` import while fixing a finding of
mine, because a pre-existing `F811` marks it redefined by a local import further down. That is a
behaviour-adjacent change I neither intended nor reviewed, so it is reverted and the pre-existing
finding stands. Ruff's baseline for the changed files is 7 before and 7 after.

## One assertion re-pinned deliberately

`test_probes.py` pins the exact key set of a serialised `ModelSpec`, and the new field joins it
with a comment saying why.

